# Caddy shares the relay network namespace (compose `network_mode:
# service:app`), so upstreams are 127.0.0.1. The app only ever talks to the
# BFF — /auth, /api, and /.well-known go there; static UI comes from the
# harness (RELAY_STATIC_DIR). Mirrors vite.config.ts dev proxying.
#
# Set RELAY_HTTPS_HOST to the public hostname for automatic HTTPS. The compose
# command refuses it unless RELAY_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1: TLS terminates here,
# in front of a loopback-bound app. Leave it empty for plain :80 (dev only —
# login needs Secure cookies, which need https). The site address comes from
# RELAY_SITE, computed by the compose command: an env placeholder default
# cannot be trusted here because a set-but-empty variable defeats it and
# Caddy rejects the resulting empty site address.
{$RELAY_SITE} {
	reverse_proxy /auth/* 127.0.0.1:8798
	reverse_proxy /api/* 127.0.0.1:8798
	reverse_proxy /.well-known/relay/* 127.0.0.1:8798
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8799
}
